id: openai
name: OpenAI-compatible

Point any OpenAI-compatible client or SDK at llm.birks.dev. These are the two variables every OpenAI SDK already reads — the official Python and Node clients, LiteLLM, LangChain, LlamaIndex, and most tools that take a custom base URL.

--- commands (sh) ---
export LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY="YOUR_API_KEY"

export OPENAI_BASE_URL="https://llm.birks.dev/v1"
export OPENAI_API_KEY="$LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY"

--- commands (PowerShell) ---
$env:LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY = "YOUR_API_KEY"

$env:OPENAI_BASE_URL = "https://llm.birks.dev/v1"
$env:OPENAI_API_KEY = $env:LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY

--- notes ---
- Set the request's "model" field to "Qwen3-Coder-30B". The same key reaches every model — only the base URL and model name change.
- The endpoint speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions API at /v1/chat/completions, which is what these clients use.
- OPENAI_API_KEY reads from $LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY so the credential stays in your environment rather than a file.

--- agent prompt ---
Configure an OpenAI-compatible client on this machine to use my self-hosted llm.birks.dev endpoint at https://llm.birks.dev. Set OPENAI_BASE_URL to https://llm.birks.dev/v1 and OPENAI_API_KEY to the credential from my environment. Use the model "Qwen3-Coder-30B". Read the API key from the LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY environment variable. Do not write the key itself into any file in a git repository, and do not print it. Preserve my existing unrelated configuration.
